        "original_id": "a5ecc25f-7b7a-50bd-82f5-96e924811839",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: M. S. Swaminathan, Norman Borlaug, Gregory Conko\n- Topics: Green Revolution in India, higher-yielding wheat varieties, genetically modified food, regulation\n- Works: The Frankenfood Myth\n- Awards: Nobel Peace Prize, Presidential Medal of Freedom, Congressional Gold Medal\n\nFacts:\n- During the Green Revolution in India, higher-yielding varieties of wheat were developed by many scientists, including Indian geneticist M. S. Swaminathan and American agronomist Norman Borlaug.\n- Norman Borlaug received multiple honors for his work, including the Nobel Peace Prize, the Presidential Medal of Freedom, and the Congressional Gold Medal.\n- The Frankenfood Myth argues against over-regulation of genetically modified food.\n- The Frankenfood Myth features a foreword by Nobel Peace Prize-winner Norman Ernest Borlaug.",
